wifi: mt76: fix wcid poll list corruption on station removal

Three system freezes on 2026-07-03 (ignavia, Framework 13 AMD, MT7925),
two with captured oopses, both identical, on kernels 7.0.11 and 7.1.2:

  wlp192s0: send auth to 80:2a:a8:52:b0:2f (try 1/3)
   slab kmalloc-rnd-11-8k start ... pointer offset 4160 size 8192
  list_add corruption. prev->next should be next (X), but was Y. (prev=Y)
  kernel BUG at lib/list_debug.c:32!

prev == prev->next means the tail node of sta_poll_list was
re-initialized (INIT_LIST_HEAD) while still linked.  The 8k slab is the
ieee80211_sta + drv_priv allocation holding the embedded mt76_wcid.

Race (mt7925, frequent roaming between APs of the same ESS):

  CPU0 (rx/txs softirq)                CPU1 (mac80211 sta teardown)
  wcid = rcu_dereference(...)
                                       rcu_assign_pointer(wcid[idx], NULL)
                                       mt76_wcid_cleanup()
                                         list_del_init(&wcid->poll_list)
  mt76_wcid_add_poll(wcid)
    wcid->sta still 1 -> re-adds
    dying wcid to sta_poll_list
                                       sta freed after RCU grace period
  ... sta_poll_list tail dangles into freed slab ...
                                       roam re-add reuses slab slot:
                                       mt76_wcid_init()
                                         INIT_LIST_HEAD(&wcid->poll_list)
                                         -> still-linked tail self-loops
  next mt76_wcid_add_poll()
    list_add_tail() -> BUG

mt76_reset_device() and the mt7915/mt7996 remove paths already clear
wcid->sta (and set sta_disabled) at teardown; the mt792x remove paths
never do, so the !wcid->sta guard in mt76_wcid_add_poll() is
ineffective there, and it runs before taking sta_poll_lock anyway.

Fix:
 - mt76_wcid_cleanup(): mark the wcid dead (sta = 0, sta_disabled = 1)
   under sta_poll_lock, in the same critical section that unlinks
   poll_list.
 - mt76_wcid_add_poll(): re-check wcid->sta under sta_poll_lock so the
   check cannot race with cleanup.
 - mt7925_mac_sta_poll(): take list_first_entry under sta_poll_lock
   (same discipline mt7921 uses); the unlocked read can race with
   cleanup unlinking the entry from the spliced private list.

diff -ruN a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c	2026-06-27 12:08:18.000000000 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c	2026-07-03 16:04:01.869430650 +0200
@@ -1727,6 +1727,13 @@
 	 * when mt76_wcid_add_poll() checks list_empty().
 	 */
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->sta_poll_lock);
+	/* Mark the wcid dead in the same critical section, so a concurrent
+	 * mt76_wcid_add_poll() from the rx/txs path cannot re-add it after
+	 * we unlink it.  Freed wcids left on sta_poll_list corrupt the list
+	 * once the slab slot is reused and re-initialized.
+	 */
+	wcid->sta = 0;
+	wcid->sta_disabled = 1;
 	if (!list_empty(&wcid->poll_list))
 		list_del_init(&wcid->poll_list);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->sta_poll_lock);
@@ -1759,7 +1766,10 @@
 		return;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->sta_poll_lock);
-	if (list_empty(&wcid->poll_list))
+	/* Re-check under the lock: mt76_wcid_cleanup() clears wcid->sta in
+	 * its sta_poll_lock section, so this cannot race with teardown.
+	 */
+	if (wcid->sta && list_empty(&wcid->poll_list))
 		list_add_tail(&wcid->poll_list, &dev->sta_poll_list);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->sta_poll_lock);
 }
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c	2026-06-27 12:08:18.000000000 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c	2026-07-03 16:04:01.869762977 +0200
@@ -46,12 +46,14 @@
 		u16 idx;
 		u8 bw;
 
-		if (list_empty(&sta_poll_list))
+		spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
+		if (list_empty(&sta_poll_list)) {
+			spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 			break;
+		}
 		mlink = list_first_entry(&sta_poll_list,
 					 struct mt792x_link_sta, wcid.poll_list);
 		msta = mlink->sta;
-		spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 		list_del_init(&mlink->wcid.poll_list);
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 
